    "answer": {
      "short": "$(a,b)=(2,2)$.\n\nFor example, rearranging gives $(a-1)(b-1)=1$, so both factors must equal $1$.",
      "worked": "Three possible proofs follow.\n\nProof 1: Assume $b\\ge a$. From $ab=a+b$,\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=\\frac{a+b}{b}\\\\a&=1+\\frac{a}{b}.\\end{align*}$$\nIf $b>a$, then $1<a<2$, contradicting that $a$ is an integer. Therefore $a=b$, so $a^2=2a$. Since $a>0$, $a=2$ and $b=2$.\n\nProof 2: Since $ab-a=b$, we have $a\\mid b$. Similarly, $ab-b=a$ gives $b\\mid a$. Positive integers that divide each other are equal, so $a=b$. Hence $a^2=2a$ and $a=b=2$.\n\nProof 3:\n$$\\begin{align*}ab-a-b&=0\\\\ab-a-b+1&=1\\\\(a-1)(b-1)&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth factors are non-negative integers, so $a-1=b-1=1$. Thus $a=b=2$.\n\nFinally, $2+2=2\\times2$, so $(2,2)$ satisfies the equation.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 118
  },
